A||||4||Frank Sombers||Door hinge pin/bushing replacement problem||||5||
Z||000000||Frank Sombers||11-24-2000||08:44 PM||||When I attempted to replace the hinge pins and bushings on my '88 Cpe. I ran into a problem. It seems that when I tried to drive out the lower pin it's head caught on the door Spring (pressure spring?) and could not be removed. Any advice on how to work through this? Also, if the spring has to be removed any ideas on how best to do that would also be appreciated.<BR>Thank you very much.<BR>Frank||||reg||5
Z||000001||2xsess||11-24-2000||09:04 PM||||Frank, there is a tool that you can buy specifically for those springs. I find that you do have to remover the springs to get the pin in . <P>Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Jeff||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||11-24-2000||09:56 PM||||Getting the springs out is easy just cover your eyes and pop it out with a big screw driver then spend about 10 min. looking for it . To install compress it and keep it compressed with a couple of cable ties, drop it into place and cut the ties. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||11-24-2000||10:13 PM||||Drop a heavy rag over the spring so it doesn't head for the neighbor's backyard via the windows. <P>I have the special tool for the spring. I'm not sure I'd try tie-wraps, but if you do USE REALLY BIG ONES. That spring could put an eye out faster than a 6 year old running with a sharp stick.<P>TK||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-24-2000||11:12 PM||||The link to the tool is in my cave, <A HREF="http://fierocave.shorturl.com" TARGET=_blank>The Fiero Cave</A>, or you can search the forum for "popping off the doors". <P>There's also notes in my cave about a hinge mod that makes them much more durable.||||reg||1
